Subject: [PATCH] avformat/bluray: open an explicitly requested playlist of any length

The protocol always listed titles with TITLES_RELEVANT and a hard-coded
180 s minimum, and failed with EIO when that list was empty, even when
-playlist named a valid playlist. Bonus features under 3 minutes, duplicate
playlists and discs with only short titles could not be opened. When a
playlist is requested explicitly, list all titles instead (libbluray still
needs bd_get_titles() before bd_select_playlist()).

Also skip a NULL bd_get_title_info() result instead of dereferencing it.
---
--- a/libavformat/bluray.c
+++ b/libavformat/bluray.c
@@ -137,8 +137,12 @@
     }
     */
 
-    /* load title list */
-    num_title_idx = bd_get_titles(bd->bd, TITLES_RELEVANT, MIN_PLAYLIST_LENGTH);
+    /* load title list: filtered when we must pick a playlist, unfiltered when one was
+     * requested explicitly (so short bonus features and duplicates can still be opened) */
+    if (bd->playlist < 0)
+        num_title_idx = bd_get_titles(bd->bd, TITLES_RELEVANT, MIN_PLAYLIST_LENGTH);
+    else
+        num_title_idx = bd_get_titles(bd->bd, TITLES_ALL, 0);
     av_log(h, AV_LOG_INFO, "%d usable playlists:\n", num_title_idx);
     if (num_title_idx < 1) {
         return AVERROR(EIO);
@@ -150,6 +154,8 @@
         int i;
         for (i = 0; i < num_title_idx; i++) {
             BLURAY_TITLE_INFO *info = bd_get_title_info(bd->bd, i, 0);
+            if (!info)
+                continue;
 
             av_log(h, AV_LOG_INFO, "playlist %05d.mpls (%d:%02d:%02d)\n",
                    info->playlist,
